  "findings": [
    "Observation-only contact instrumentation reproduced both accepted motion captures exactly.",
    "Opposing sequential contact normals occur on the same joint, including a calf guard and a fold guard with dot product about -0.856. This supports contact conflict, not a complete causal diagnosis.",
    "Some offset directional capsules do not intersect the anatomical capsule. Rest-clear enclosing capsules preserve old volume but did not alone improve both motion clips.",
    "A no-contact diagnostic reduced Walk direction-jerk p95 by 28.6 percent but increased Run p95 by 4.3 percent. Run sharp motion is not explained solely by collision responses; do not present the diagnostic as a usable setup.",
    "All-collider overlap mixes anatomical contact, directional support, and virtual fold/sector buffers. Keep those measurements distinct from actual mesh intersections.",
    "Upper-only drag improved typical motion and anatomical-capsule overlap but increased peak Walk jerk; it is not accepted.",
    "Enclosing guards plus drag 0.65 improved p95 direction jerk about 40 percent in both clips, but reintroduced strap crossings and increased the Walk anatomical-capsule maximum. Rejected."
  ],
  "metric_limits": [
    "Direction jerk is the third sample difference of world bone directions at 24 fps after initial exclusion; it includes authored parent motion and is not a physical jerk unit.",
    "Anatomical-capsule measurements exclude directional and overlay guards, use the same original capsule shapes for every candidate, and verify unchanged kinematic bone heads before comparison.",
    "The broad non-secondary mesh partition includes body-attached clothing. Its triangle-intersection counts are diagnostic, not a clean skin-only penetration guarantee.",
    "No-contact capture arrays contain zero contacts because references were cleared. Those zeros must never be treated as zero penetration; the shared-reference anatomical check correctly reports large overlap.",
    "These are disposable Grace Walk/Run tests, not all-character, Windows, live UI, drag, or visual acceptance."
